From 148d9676769eaf6d459466a810d31b23c35d1918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:53:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ftrace: Prefer objtool mcount recording where it can
 write NOPs

When the compiler accepts -mrecord-mcount, FTRACE_MCOUNT_USE_CC is
selected and objtool does not record the __fentry__ call sites. The
compiler leaves those sites as calls, so ftrace_init() has to turn
every one of them into a NOP at boot, in ftrace_update_code().

objtool records the same sites and, on architectures that select
HAVE_OBJTOOL_NOP_MCOUNT, writes the NOPs at build time (--mnop). The
build then defines CC_USING_NOP_MCOUNT, ftrace_need_init_nop() is
false, and the boot-time conversion does not happen.

Make FTRACE_MCOUNT_USE_CC depend on !HAVE_OBJTOOL_NOP_MCOUNT, so the
objtool path is taken wherever it can write the NOPs.

On an x86_64 KVM guest with one vCPU (gcc 14.2, about 41,000 fentry
sites) this takes 7.0 ms off the time from kernel start to "Freeing
unused kernel image": p50 of 15 boots, interleaved with the unpatched
kernel. The function tracer, function_graph and fentry/fexit BPF
programs work as before.

The cost is at build time: objtool records the sites of every object,
which the compiler did before.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/trace/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/trace/Kconfig b/kernel/trace/Kconfig
index 084f34dc6..7aae107f2 100644
--- a/kernel/trace/Kconfig
+++ b/kernel/trace/Kconfig
@@ -883,6 +883,7 @@ config FTRACE_MCOUNT_USE_CC
 	depends on $(cc-option,-mrecord-mcount)
 	depends on !FTRACE_MCOUNT_USE_PATCHABLE_FUNCTION_ENTRY
 	depends on DYNAMIC_FTRACE
+	depends on !HAVE_OBJTOOL_NOP_MCOUNT
 
 config FTRACE_MCOUNT_USE_OBJTOOL
 	def_bool y
